<title>USA: SRI LANKA BUYS 50,000 T OPTIONAL SOFT WHEAT - TRADE.</title>
<headline>SRI LANKA BUYS 50,000 T OPTIONAL SOFT WHEAT - TRADE.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sri Lanka bought on Thursday night 50,000 tonnes optional origin soft red wheat for August shipment, several U.S. exporters said.  </p>
<p>Several exporters said the wheat was slated for August 18 to August 27 delivery.</p>
<p>&quot;They tendered and bought last night,&quot; one U.S. exporter said.</p>
<p>He said the wheat was purchased at around $168.00 a tonne, cost and freight.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel 312-983-7305))</p>
</text>
